{
  "source": "the shootGuard gate stands at the original cell [26, 15] facing right with the crane key behind it, blocks the hero until destroyed, fires 18-shot bursts (the original takes 18 energy per burst) and takes only E-Blaster beam ticks (shootable.by beam, 60 ticks: the original 20 hits against 5 per droid, here droids take 15) (docs/research/reports/10-level1-enemies.md, Guards drawn and firing); the acidGuard gate fires droid bursts (fires: facing, burst, pauseMs, states it fires in) at a hero it sees on its floor until the acid wrecks it; the original plays its firing clip, takes 5 energy and pushes the hero back one cell when the hero enters cols 103-119 on its floor (KLEV1.EXE 3:0xDF10-0xE429), here droid bullets instead (user); item props at the centre of the original pickup window (hero engine x X-2..X, map col X+6, so x = col - 0.5) from docs/research/reports/13-level1-layout.md; object cells from docs/research/reports/10-level1-enemies.md markers and the M12-M16 diffs, refined on docs/research/gamedata/png/maps/map_M11.png (bar door col 39, train door cols 60-61, switchboard on the pillar at col 69, valve wheel col 43 row 73, acid tank outlet cols 111-112, crane winch cols 39-40 on floor 10, code lock panel col 115 row 42); blocking cells equal map.json taskWalls; metroTunnel, waterPipe and plasmaBarrier are gates (no use, opened by sets); scenery laid out by Claude over map_M11.png with the closest env asset, x is the asset left edge, y the floor row; object art is centred on the use x, `art` (cells) moves it onto the original art (valve wheel, ship, card door, acid tank, and the crane beam over the gap at cols 23-31 row 13); damagedLift draws the liftPanel asset (state 1 damaged, 0 repaired) since the map lift draws the lift itself; metroTunnel draws tunnelGate (our own look, the original gate is an invisible task wall): a wall the train runs behind, between the train door and the always open middle door of the trainCarriage (a closed door at its far end); the crowbar opens only the train door and with it the gate; `cover` clips the hero out of the train body and the open door leaves between the doors (clip) while his centre is in a doorway or inside (reach, `states` gates it on the prop state), keeps enemy patrols out of reach, and stops an airborne hero from entering the train or a hero inside from jumping, so he passes the wall inside the train (user); the crane chain runs `art.top` 13 cells up to the map top; a liftPanel dressing marks the crane winch use spot, where the original crane mast wall stood (user); ground is the street floor row, the rows under it are underground and draw darker, with stripLight tubes mounted on the metro ceiling (user)",
